{"actor":"store","data":{"by_calls":["call-ae0b8cad4763","call-1e1045f1291b","job-a1dda38b573d","job-3c3aff86bc2b","job-3d352f906661","call-b0f9a87d5080","job-fb373286ef1b","job-991076bcf18c","job-2fd37e205c15","job-8f521952bf4d","job-ae37369e4459","job-0328f5f46b05","job-c245a5c7a5b1","job-5ce0917e19f9","job-8aab0e48e0d8","call-710db4a4d437","call-226ec5daddc5"],"card_id":"card-c9615069","card_version":2,"reasons":["gate rule: disproof","confirmed disproof of 'Secondary prediction: median over 5 seeds of pretraining sequences before held-out one-shot recall reaches 0.95 is <= 3000 (Adam lr 1e-2, batch 32); gate closure rho<=kappa for filler/bridge pairs': 3000 sequences at batch 32 is about 94 Adam steps. Adam moves each raw parameter by roughly lr per step, so at most about 0.94 in raw units. Initialise with r=8 and E_i=F_j chosen so that k=E.F=1, which gives softplus entries of 0.354 and raw about -0.857. Even if every raw entry of E and F moves down by 0.94, the minimum reachable k is about 0.19 and rho is about 0.16, which is far above kappa=1e","confirmed disproof of 'For K = 32, all stored records have the equal concentration rho, so each new complex beyond 16 evicts the record with the smallest tau, which is the oldest. The last 16 pairs score >= 0.9 and the firs': Trained rho_ij = k/(1+k) varies by pair, for example in [0.9, 0.99]. For 32 disjoint fresh pairs, the records have C = rho_ij. Eviction by (smallest C, then oldest tau) removes the smallest-rho record, not the oldest. The newly written record can even evict itself. The survivors then are not the last 16, so many early pairs stay at high recall and many late pairs drop to about 0. The 'last 16 >= 0","round 1 feasibility_judge_a (claude-opus-5-5): infeasible (confidence 0.85); fatal: Capacity claim for K = 32 with P_max = 16 is refuted. Eviction by min(C, tau) removes the smallest-concentration record, not the oldest, because trained rho_ij = E_i·F_j / (1 + E_i·F_j) differs across pairs. A replayed executed check showed survivors other than the last 16 pairs, including cases where a just-written pair evicts itself, so the 'last 16 >= 0.9, first 16 <= 0.15' split fails.; The le","round 1 feasibility_judge_b (qwen3.6-35b-a3b-mlx): infeasible (confidence 0.95); fatal: Eviction logic fails to preserve recency when rho varies, and K=32 exceeds index bit capacity.; Learnability check proves gate closure to kappa=1e-3 is impossible in 3000 sequences, breaking filler robustness and one-shot recall assumptions.; Cross-ratio claim fails at high rho because pruning deletes necessary cells, making the ratio undefined.","obligation check complexity_time_memory_total (complexity): discharged (replayed): Per-token op tally from the card steps is T = 7*P + V + r + 5, which has no n. Since 12(V+P+r) - T = 5*P + 11*V + 11*r - 5 has nonnegative coefficients, T is O(V+P+r) with c=12. This counts the stated steps, not measured time, and it does not model the dense V-array cost beyond counting V once.","obligation check capacity_one_shot_recall_K8_and_P_max (capacity): violated (replayed): Index-bit capacity: state 16 records x 11 bits = 176 bits; required 6K bits = {8: 48, 16: 96, 32: 192}. K<=16 fits, and K=32 (192 bits) does not, so full recall of 32 is impossible. Eviction by min (C, tau) with rho drawn uniformly in [0.9,0.99] (an assumed range) on 32 disjoint pairs: the survivors; counterexample {\"trial\": 0, \"rhos\": [0.976, 0.9682, 0.9379, 0.9233, 0.946, 0.9364, 0.9705, 0.9273, 0.9429, 0.9525, 0.9817, 0.9454, 0.9254, 0.968, 0.9557, 0.9225, 0.9819, 0.9885, 0.9729, 0.9812, 0.9279, 0.9657, 0.9809, 0.9616, 0.9425, 0.9091, 0.9391, 0.955, 0.9822, 0.987, 0.9429, 0.9779], \"survivors\": [[0, 32], [1,","obligation check capacity_filler_robustness (numerical_stability): not_checked [checkable kind, but the checker wrote no program]","obligation check binding_exchange_algebra (algebraic): discharged (replayed): Symbolic pulse recursion with one shared rho: stream q a r a gives residuals C_ra-rho, C_qa-rho(1-rho), y_a-(1-rho)^2, and stream q a q b gives C_qb-rho, C_qa-rho(1-rho); all simplify to 0. The readout inequalities p(a|r)>=0.9 and p(a|q)<=0.15 are not checked here.","obligation check elimination_routing_gap (numerical_stability): unknown: With rho=0.9 and uniform u over 64 values, p(v8)=0.5882 at eta=0. The mean-probability claim p>=0.35 holds only for eta <= 0.0189. The ablation with u alone gives 0.0156. The trained eta and u are not known to this program, so the claim is not decided.","obligation check order_dependence_cross_ratio (algebraic): unknown: The toy reproduces at rho=0.5. Gaps at rho 0.9, 0.95, 0.99 are at least 0.2 where cells survive pruning; cells pruned at rhos [0.99]. The claim covers all rho in [0.9,1), which is not exhausted, and the per-cell Sinkhorn part is not computed.","obligation check learnability_rate_prior (learnability): not_checked","obligation check numerical_validity_and_well_definedness (numerical_stability): unknown: Float64 recursion on 10 random streams of length 1000 with V=16 and P_max=16 gave min free mass 0 and max row-sum excess 0. This is a sample, not a proof over all n, so it cannot discharge the claim."],"stage":"S3","verdict":"infeasible_proved"},"hash":"cbdcd15b733b81bfe17fccc596df14e705d8c64bd16bde6a8acdba448268aa29","prev_hash":"02c49264f91bea3738f5e32b0c5cc71733dbb55aa146a0c4b52714a7d6944730","seq":40,"ts":"2026-10-11T02:13:08.202323+00:00","type":"verdict"}
